#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Wave 38: Little Hands, Just Three, a Ninth Time — the closing wave.

Eight consecutive 3-only waves have narrowed the age-3 / age-4
gap 102 -> 90 -> 78 -> 66 -> 54 -> 42 -> 30 -> 18 -> 6. This
wave does NOT repeat the twelve-record shape: the gap is six
wide, so the pack is six records — exactly the six, no padding
to a familiar number. Six more records banded 3-3 (short,
<= 20 minutes, adult-led, big pieces, one rule per game), aimed
at the six lowest age-3 primary counts measured before the wave:
holidays 12 and team-community 12 (the floor), then seasons,
stem, icebreakers and outdoor at 13 each. Result, asserted in
the wave log: age 3 154 -> 160, age 4 unchanged at 160, the
headline gap 6 -> 0 — closed, at parity, by records the threes
own outright — and every primary category now carries at least
13 age-3 primaries (the floor rises 12 -> 13 in the same wave).

Drafts cut before running, recorded rather than padded over
(the wave-37 discipline): a bird-listening minute for the
outdoor slot — bird-call-count already counts calls at 5-14 and
the cut-down is the same game, not a younger ceremony; a
lemonade-stand pouring record for the seasons slot —
pouring-practice-trays already teaches pouring at 3-5, and a
paper hat does not make it a new record. Both slots were
rebuilt: the outdoor slot became the mud pie bakery (no bakery
anywhere on the shelf) and the seasons slot became the
sandcastle (no sandcastle anywhere on the shelf either).

Deliberate neighbours, kept on purpose and named here:
- big-groundhog-shadow-morning-look vs big-shadow-grow-shrink
  (3-only, stem — making a shadow grow and shrink is play WITH
  a shadow you already have): nothing is grown or shrunk here —
  the group checks whether a shadow is out at all on one named
  morning, and reports the morning in two words.
- big-new-friend-room-tour vs big-picnic-blanket-set-together
  (a crew setting one place together): the blanket there is
  set; the room here is SHOWN — three places a new person
  needs, pointed at and named by the children who live there.
- big-sandcastle-one-bucket-towers vs big-funnel-sand-pour
  (sand poured through a funnel, stem): pouring is the funnel's
  whole record; here wet sand is moulded, turned out, counted
  and decorated — the sand stands, which is the opposite lesson.
- big-sound-jar-loud-or-soft vs big-smell-jar-sniff-and-say
  (3-only, stem — one sniff, say what the nose found): the nose
  there, the ear here; nothing is guessed in either — a jar is
  shaken once and filed by its loudness on the right mat.
- big-choose-your-colour-corner vs big-feelings-card-show-and-say
  (a card shown, a feeling named): feelings there are named
  from cards; here a favourite colour is chosen with the feet,
  stood in, and allowed to change in the open.
- big-mud-pie-bakery-morning vs big-pot-stir-together (3-only,
  rainy-day — one big pot stirred in turn, indoors): the pot
  there is pretend cooking at a table; the pies here are real
  mud, mixed outdoors to a tested thickness, and returned to
  the garden bed when the bakery closes.

The drama/coding lane, recorded not padded (standing rule):
there is still no drama or coding category in the archive's
eleven, and no tag in the validator's vocabulary names one.
This wave does not invent a twelfth category to look complete.
The lane stays on the record as an honest gap.

Safety notes are practical only — no medical claims anywhere.

Run once: dedupes by id, writes data/activities.json only
(collections unchanged this wave — see the note above the pack).
Run scripts/build.py afterwards.
"""
